cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SCM-BH: Jet Structure and Doppler-Regime Modulation in MOJAVE AGN"
message: "If you use this analysis or data, please cite it as below."
type: dataset

authors:
  - family-names: "Cámara Madrid"
    given-names: "Sergio"

doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19736765

repository-code: "https://github.com/sergiocamaramadrid-cyber/Motor-de-Velos-SCM"

version: "scm-bh-v0.1"

keywords:
  - astrophysics
  - AGN
  - jet geometry
  - MOJAVE
  - Doppler factor
  - black hole mass
  - Eddington ratio
  - reproducibility

abstract: >
  Exploratory SCM-BH analysis of AGN jet geometry using MOJAVE jet-opening measurements
  and Wu & Shen DR16Q physical properties. Main result: observed jet opening angles are
  dominated by intrinsic structural scale r15; black-hole mass, bolometric luminosity, and
  Eddington ratio show no robust direct or residual correlations. A secondary Doppler-regime
  modulation is detected with a low-δ / high-δ transition.

license: "MIT"

date-released: 2026-04-24
